Pierre Abbat wrote:
> There's a gismu creating program which I've looked at, but couldn't figure out 
> how to use. Where is it, and how can I use it?

The only one I know is the one we used to make the gismu originally, 
written in Turbo Pascal 4 or something.  Last we tried, it no longer 
would compile under the current TP version, and the original compiled 
version no longer ran, being an old fashioned DOS program, I think with 
hand-coded 8086 assembler embedded for the tightest loop.  It is 
plausible that it would run under DOSBOX or something, but there hasn't 
been enough reason to make the effort.

We still have source and object.  It is probably also on lojban.org 
smewhere.

